      "content": "Your exhaustion makes perfect sense after pushing your athletic limits for so long; the silence of everyday life can feel jarring when you're used to the roar of crowds and high-energy environments. It's a common transition phase for former athletes as they adapt to a new normal where the instinct to perform no longer matches their current reality. Remember that healing isn't linear, and finding new ways to engage with your environment slowly takes time and patience.",
